{%- liquid
  assign columns = section.settings.columns_desktop | default: 4
  assign desktop_vw = 100 | divided_by: columns
  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 990px) ' | append: desktop_vw | append: 'vw, (min-width: 640px) 33vw, 50vw'

  assign terms = search.terms | escape
-%}

{%- paginate search.results by 250 -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Brands are matched here rather than read out of `search.results`: the
  storefront search endpoint returns products only, whatever `type` asks for, so
  a brand a shopper typed by name would otherwise be the one thing the results
  page could not find. The suggestions panel gets them from the predictive
  endpoint, which does index collections.

  Matched on the handleized title rather than the raw one, which is what makes
  the comparison survive this catalogue: handleize folds accents, drops
  apostrophes and collapses punctuation and spaces to single hyphens, so
  "vontelle" finds Vontélle Eyewear, "ljai" finds L'Jai Amor and "silk noir"
  finds Silk + Noir. On the title, not `collection.handle` — the stored handles
  drift from the titles here, typos included.

  Walking `collections` is the same cost the A–Z brand directory already pays on
  every page.

  Captured up here, ahead of the markup, because the result count in the page
  header has to include them.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign brand_count = 0 -%}
{%- capture brand_items -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    `contains ''` is true of every string, so a blank term would list the whole
    brand roster.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if search.performed and search.terms != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The entities are unpicked before the handle is built. `search.terms`
      arrives HTML-escaped, so an apostrophe reaches this as `&#39;` and
      handleize renders that as "-39-" — searching L'Jai Amor produced
      `l-39-jai` and matched nothing. Ampersands go the same way via `&amp;`.

      Apostrophes are then dropped on both sides rather than handleized,
      because handleize does not treat the two characters alike: it discards a
      curly ’ and turns a straight ' into a hyphen, which is enough on its own
      to make the two strings disagree.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign needle = search.terms
      | replace: '&#39;', ''
      | replace: '&#8217;', ''
      | replace: '&amp;', ' '
      | replace: "'", ''
      | replace: '’', ''
      | handleize
    -%}
    {%- for collection in collections -%}
      {%- if collection.metafields.custom.type.value == 'Brand' -%}
        {%- assign brand_title = collection.title | replace: "'", '' | replace: '’', '' | handleize -%}
        {%- if brand_title contains needle -%}
          {%- assign brand_count = brand_count | plus: 1 -%}
          <li>
            <a class="search-results__brand" href="{{ collection.url }}">{{ collection.title }}</a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture product_items -%}
  {%- for item in search.results -%}
    {%- liquid
      # `render` takes values, not expressions, so the comparison has to
      # resolve to a variable before it is passed down.
      assign lazy_card = false
      if forloop.index > 8
        assign lazy_card = true
      endif
    -%}
    {%- render 'product-card', product: item, lazy: lazy_card, sizes: card_sizes -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- assign total_count = search.results_count | plus: brand_count -%}

<div class="search-results">

  {%- comment -%}
    The term itself is the page title, the way a collection's name is — an h1
    reading "Results for …" runs to three lines at --text-7xl.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <header class="search-results__header">
    <p class="search-results__eyebrow">{{ 'templates.search.title' | t }}</p>
    <h1 class="search-results__title">
      {%- if search.performed -%}
        {{- terms -}}
      {%- else -%}
        {{- 'templates.search.prompt' | t -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    </h1>

    {%- comment -%}
      Repeated here rather than leaving it to the header bar: this is where a
      shopper who got nothing back will retype, and on a phone the header bar
      has scrolled away by then.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign focus_form = false
      unless search.performed
        assign focus_form = true
      endunless
    -%}
    <div class="search-results__form">
      {%- render 'search-form',
        input_id: 'search-page-input',
        modifier: 'page',
        autofocus: focus_form
      -%}
    </div>

    {%- if search.performed -%}
      <p class="search-results__count">
        {{- 'templates.search.results_count' | t: count: total_count -}}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </header>

  {%- if search.performed -%}

    {%- if brand_items != blank -%}
      <section class="search-results__group" aria-labelledby="search-brands-heading">
        <h2 class="search-results__group-title" id="search-brands-heading">
          {{- 'general.search.brands' | t -}}
        </h2>
        <ul class="search-results__brands">
          {{ brand_items }}
        </ul>
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if product_items != blank -%}
      <section class="search-results__group" aria-labelledby="search-products-heading">
        <h2 class="search-results__group-title" id="search-products-heading">
          {{- 'general.search.products' | t -}}
        </h2>
        <div class="search-results__grid" style="--columns-desktop: {{ columns }};">
          {{ product_items }}
        </div>
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      A term as ordinary as "noir" already returns close to 500 products, so
      unlike the collection grid this page genuinely runs past one page and
      needs a way forward. Prev/next rather than numbered pages: the theme has
      no pagination component and result 400 is not a place anyone navigates to
      directly.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if paginate.pages > 1 -%}
      <nav class="search-results__pagination" aria-label="{{ 'templates.search.pagination' | t }}">
        {%- if paginate.previous -%}
          <a class="search-results__page-link" href="{{ paginate.previous.url }}" rel="prev">
            {%- render 'icon', name: 'chevron-left' -%}
            {{ 'templates.search.previous' | t }}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}

        <span class="search-results__page-count">
          {{- 'templates.search.page_of' | t: current: paginate.current_page, total: paginate.pages -}}
        </span>

        {%- if paginate.next -%}
          <a class="search-results__page-link" href="{{ paginate.next.url }}" rel="next">
            {{ 'templates.search.next' | t }}
            {%- render 'icon', name: 'chevron-right' -%}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if total_count == 0 -%}
      <div class="search-results__empty">
        <p>{{ 'general.search.no_results' | t: terms: terms }}</p>
        <p class="search-results__empty-hint">{{ 'templates.search.empty_hint' | t }}</p>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

  {%- endif -%}

</div>

{%- endpaginate -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Search",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_desktop",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 5,
      "label": "Columns (desktop)"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
